diff --git a/docs/PROFILES.md b/docs/PROFILES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f84f52
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/PROFILES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@
+# Profiles and Stack Configs
+
+This repo boots via **profile-driven stacks**:
+
+```powershell
+python -m steuerung3d up --profile 1dev_sim
+```
+
+Profiles are TOML files under:
+
+- `configs/stacks/*.toml`  (stack profiles)
+- `configs/services/*.toml` (service defaults / app configs)
+
+The supervisor expands the stack TOML into one or more processes, each with its own args, logging, and session folder.
+
+---
+
+## Stack file structure (`configs/stacks/<name>.toml`)
+
+Typical sections:
+
+### `[stack]`
+- `name` (string): profile name
+
+### `[rig]`
+Defines the rig context that other sections interpolate.
+
+Common keys:
+- `axes` (array[string]): axis ids (e.g. `["Anton"]`)
+- `device_source` (string): `"sim"` or `"real"` (policy/config usage)
+
+### `[net]`
+Defines local bind host and the standard port bases used across services.
+
+Common keys:
+- `bind_host`
+- `cmd_base` (base port for device CommandOut)
+- `ui_telem_base` (base port for UI TelemetryOut)
+- `dev_telem_in` (host:port for Core to bind and receive device telemetry)
+- `intent` (host:port for Core intent input)
+- `raw_in`, `status_in` (optional seams)
+
+### `[services.<name>]`
+Each service declares:
+- `enabled` (bool)
+- `module` (python module path)
+- `mode` (string): `"single"` or `"per_axis"`
+- `config` (optional): TOML config passed to service
+- `count` (optional int): number of instances (for `"single"` mode)
+- `args` (array[string]): argv list, supporting interpolation
+
+Example:
+
+```toml
+[services.core]
+enabled = true
+module = "steuerung3d.apps.core_udp_service"
+mode = "single"
+args = [
+  "--intent-in", "{net.intent}",
+  "--dev-telem-in", "{net.dev_telem_in}",
+  "--dev-cmd-base", "{net.cmd_base}",
+  "--dev-cmd-count", "{len(rig.axes)}",
+  "--ui-telem-base", "{net.ui_telem_base}",
+  "--ui-telem-count", "{len(rig.axes)}",
+  "{repeat('--axis', rig.axes)}",
+]
+```
+
+---
+
+## Interpolation rules
+
+The stack supervisor expands placeholders inside `{...}`.
+
+Common patterns you will see:
+- `{net.intent}` – reference another section key
+- `{len(rig.axes)}` – length of list
+- `{axis}` / `{axis_index}` – per-axis expansion in `mode="per_axis"`
+- `{repeat('--axis', rig.axes)}` – repeat an option for each axis
+- `{csv(rig.axes)}` – comma-separated list
+
+These are intentionally simple and explicit: stack files should remain readable and diff-friendly.
+
+---
+
+## Service configs (`configs/services/*.toml`)
+
+Service configs are “app-level defaults”:
+
+- `configs/services/densi.toml`
+- `configs/services/hip.toml`
+
+They keep stack files small and focus stacks on wiring.
+
+---
+
+## Recommended conventions
+
+1) Prefer `mode="per_axis"` for anything that must be axis-pinned (DenSi).
+2) Keep Core as `mode="single"` and route strictly per-axis at the edges.
+3) Avoid implicit defaults for multi-axis networking:
+   - if `rig.axes` has more than one axis, require explicit per-axis targets.
+4) Document new profiles by copying an existing stack and changing only the minimal wiring.
+
+
